Frankly I have no idea what upstream is even doing.
I also can't find any issues about this on their tracker.

Without this patch, we get:

ERROR: /build/tensorflow/src/tensorflow-2.21.0-cuda/tensorflow/core/common_runtime/BUILD:1716:11: Compiling tensorflow/core/common_runtime/renamed_device.cc failed: undeclared inclusion(s) in rule '//tensorflow/core/common_runtime:renamed_device':
this rule is missing dependency declarations for the following files included by 'tensorflow/core/common_runtime/renamed_device.cc':
  'external/xla/xla/tsl/concurrency/executor.h'

Apparently this is how we can make bazel add the missed dependency.
I can't imagine this somehow magically builds on upstream without this patch.
We even use the same fucking bazel version.

